-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\">## this code is working well for all imputed datasets (not just for the first one)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>modelMI_imp1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sem</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">myModelSEM</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dataMI$imputations</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ordered</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;bi1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;bi2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;bi3&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;bi4&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;bi5&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">modelMI_imp1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">measures</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> standardized</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Well, if all the data sets can be analyzed fine, the problem might be with combining results, but I&#39;m not sure why that would be happening.  I&#39;m curious to see what will happen after you update semTools and make your imputation model consistent with your analysis model.  You already have to use DWLS because of your binary indicators, but if you want to impute the 5-category items as ordered, treat them as ordered in the analysis too, or treat them as continuous in both.</div><div><br></div><div>Terry</div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div>"
